      "title": "The Object Database Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Object Database Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Content-addressable store",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Key = ==SHA-1== of the content (40 hex chars)",
                "Value = the object, kept in `.git/objects/ab/cdef...`",
                "ID = SHA-1 of `type size\\0` + content",
                "Same content = same hash, so it is {green:stored once}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "echo 'test content' | git hash-object -w --stdin"
              ],
              "note": "-w writes the blob into .git/objects"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "d670460b4b4aece5915caf5c68d12f560a9fe3e4"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Four object types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Holds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**blob**",
                  "file bytes, no name"
                ],
                [
                  "**tree**",
                  "directory listing"
                ],
                [
                  "**commit**",
                  "snapshot pointer + metadata"
                ],
                [
                  "**tag**",
                  "annotated, named pointer"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. How they link",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Commit",
                    "sub": "tree + parent commits",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Tree",
                    "sub": "blobs + sub-trees",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Blob",
                    "sub": "file bytes",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Objects are immutable",
              "text": "Change one byte and the ==hash changes==. 'Editing' always creates a **new object**; the old one stays."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Blobs, Trees, Commits and Tags",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Blobs, Trees, Commits and Tags",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Blob and tree entry",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Blob== = file contents only, no name",
                "Name and mode live in the **parent tree entry**",
                "Entry format: `mode type hash name`",
                "Rename = new tree entry, {green:no new blob}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Type",
                "Means"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`100644`",
                  "blob",
                  "file"
                ],
                [
                  "`100755`",
                  "blob",
                  "executable"
                ],
                [
                  "`120000`",
                  "blob",
                  "symlink"
                ],
                [
                  "`040000`",
                  "tree",
                  "directory"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Commit and tag",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Commit: ==tree== hash, ==parent== hash(es), author, committer, message",
                "{blue:Root commit}: no parent",
                "{purple:Merge commit}: two or more parents",
                "{orange:Lightweight tag}: just a ref to a commit",
                "{green:Annotated tag}: real object with tagger, date, message"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git tag -a v1.0 -m 'msg'"
              ],
              "note": "annotated tag"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Reuse by hash",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Unchanged subtree keeps its hash, so it is ==reused==",
                "A new commit adds objects only for what **changed**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A commit points to one root ==tree== plus its parents."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Refs, HEAD and the Index",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Refs, HEAD and the Index",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Branches and HEAD",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Branch = file `.git/refs/heads/<name>` with ==one commit hash==",
                "Creating a branch writes ==41 bytes==: 40 hex + newline",
                "HEAD is normally a ==symbolic ref==: `ref: refs/heads/main`",
                "{red:Detached HEAD} = HEAD holds a raw commit hash"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Risk: commits made detached are lost once you switch away",
                "Recover: `git reflog` → `git branch <name> <sha>`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Index",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Index== = staging area, binary file `.git/index`",
                "Lists path, mode, blob hash and stat info for the next commit"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "git add",
                    "sub": "hash the file",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Write blob",
                    "sub": "object store",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Update entry",
                    "sub": "in the index",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Status and Reflog",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Compares",
                "Shows"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git status`",
                  "HEAD vs index",
                  "staged"
                ],
                [
                  "`git status`",
                  "index vs working tree",
                  "unstaged"
                ],
                [
                  "`git reflog`",
                  "HEAD and refs history",
                  "lost commits"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why can a detached commit be lost?** Nothing points to it, so gc can prune it; reflog still finds it",
                "**What does git add write?** A blob in the object store, then the index entry"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How a Commit Is Built and Packed",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "How a Commit Is Built and Packed",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Building a commit",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "hash-object + update-index",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "write-tree",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "commit-tree",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "update-ref",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git add` = hash-object + update-index",
                "`git commit` = write-tree, commit-tree, update-ref"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "sha=$(echo hi | git hash-object -w --stdin)",
                "git update-index --add --cacheinfo 100644,$sha,a.txt",
                "tree=$(git write-tree)",
                "c=$(git commit-tree $tree -m msg)",
                "git update-ref refs/heads/main $c"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Hashes chain history",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Hash covers ==tree, parents, author, dates, message==",
                "Change an ancestor: every descendant hash changes",
                "Amend: makes a new commit",
                "Children of the old commit still point to the old one"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Packing",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Loose",
                "Pack"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Layout",
                  "one zlib file each",
                  "`.pack` + `.idx`"
                ],
                [
                  "Made by",
                  "each write",
                  "`git gc` / `git repack`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Similar objects stored as ==deltas== vs a base: repo grows far slower than its snapshots",
                "==Unreachable== = no branch, tag, HEAD or reflog entry reaches it",
                "`git gc` prunes unreachable objects after the 2-week expiry"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Plumbing Commands and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Plumbing Commands and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Inspect and Write Objects",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git cat-file -t <sha>`",
                  "prints the ==type=="
                ],
                [
                  "`git cat-file -s <sha>`",
                  "prints the size"
                ],
                [
                  "`git cat-file -p HEAD`",
                  "pretty-prints content (the commit)"
                ],
                [
                  "`git hash-object <file>`",
                  "prints the hash only"
                ],
                [
                  "`git ls-tree -r HEAD`",
                  "root tree; `-r` recurses subtrees"
                ],
                [
                  "`git ls-files -s`",
                  "index entries"
                ],
                [
                  "`git rev-parse HEAD`",
                  "name to full hash"
                ],
                [
                  "`git show-ref`",
                  "lists all refs"
                ],
                [
                  "`git verify-pack -v <idx>`",
                  "inspects a pack"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`hash-object` alone writes nothing; add ==-w== to store the blob in the object database"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Myth",
                "Truth"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Branch contains commits",
                  "It points to **one tip**; commits live in the object database"
                ],
                [
                  "Deleted branch = commits gone",
                  "They survive until `gc` prunes them after ==gc.pruneExpire== (2 weeks)"
                ],
                [
                  "SHA-1 is a signature",
                  "It identifies content; only {green:signed} commits and tags prove the author"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Losing commits for good",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "reflog expire",
                    "note": "`--expire=now --all`",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "gc --prune=now",
                    "note": "deletes unreachable",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Gone",
                    "note": "no recovery path",
                    "ink": "black"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never",
              "text": "Run `gc --prune=now` or delete files in `.git/objects` by hand: it destroys the ==reflog== recovery path."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Git Internals Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Git Internals Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Objects and refs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Holds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==blob==",
                  "file bytes"
                ],
                [
                  "==tree==",
                  "directory"
                ],
                [
                  "==commit==",
                  "snapshot + parents"
                ],
                [
                  "==tag==",
                  "annotated name"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stored at `.git/objects/xx/yyyy`",
                "`.git/refs/heads/*`, `.git/refs/tags/*`",
                "==HEAD== = symbolic ref or raw hash",
                "Reflog: `.git/logs`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Inspect and write",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Inspect",
                "Command"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Type / size / content",
                  "`cat-file -t / -s / -p <sha>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Tree of HEAD",
                  "`ls-tree -r HEAD`"
                ],
                [
                  "Index",
                  "`ls-files -s`"
                ],
                [
                  "Name to hash",
                  "`rev-parse HEAD`"
                ],
                [
                  "All refs",
                  "`show-ref`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "hash-object -w",
                    "sub": "blob",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "update-index --add --cacheinfo",
                    "sub": "index",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "write-tree",
                    "sub": "tree",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "commit-tree",
                    "sub": "commit",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "update-ref",
                    "sub": "branch moves",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Storage",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Loose: one ==zlib== file per object",
                "`git gc` / `repack` → `.pack` + `.idx`",
                "Packs use ==delta compression=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Plain `git gc` prunes unreachable objects only past `gc.pruneExpire` (2 weeks); `--prune=now` skips it",
                "Amend adds one commit, old children stay; ==rebase== rewrites every descendant hash"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Branch = pointer",
              "text": "One commit hash, 41 bytes. Commits outlive branch deletion until gc."
            }
          ]
        }
